# TEMPLATE — do not edit the rendered patches/llm-egress-cluster-cidrs.yaml (gitignored).
# deploy/scripts/minikube-detect-cluster-cidrs.sh renders this file, replacing
# __K8S_API_CIDRS__ and __CLUSTER_INTERNAL_CIDRS__ with the live cluster values.
# Committing real CIDRs here would dirty every contributor's tree and bake one
# environment's pod/service CIDRs into a shared manifest — they differ between a
# dev minikube and prod (distinct pod/Service CIDRs, apiserver reachability).
#
# WHAT THIS ENABLES — the "strong" cluster-internal guard on the egress broker.
# HCC's openaiEgressBrokerReconciler rejects an operator baseURL that points at a
# cluster-internal address so a local-model Host cannot be turned into an SSRF
# pivot into the control plane. That guard has two tiers:
#
#   * ALWAYS ON (no config): the baseURL must be a private, non-reserved RFC1918
#     address, and the runtime `/32` egress NetworkPolicy HCC emits already pins
#     the one LAN destination — a broker can reach nothing else outbound.
#   * STRONG (needs these envs): when CONTEXT_MAPPER_K8S_API_CIDRS and/or
#     CONTEXT_MAPPER_CLUSTER_INTERNAL_CIDRS are set, HCC additionally rejects a
#     baseURL whose IP falls inside the apiserver / pod / Service CIDRs, which CEL
#     in the CRD cannot compute (no CIDR arithmetic). Without them HCC does NOT
#     fail closed at boot — it simply runs the always-on tier.
#
# This patch is OPT-IN. It is intentionally NOT listed in the overlay's
# patchesStrategicMerge by default, because the placeholders below are not valid
# CIDRs and an invalid value WOULD make HCC fail at boot. To turn the strong
# guard on for an environment:
#   1. Render real values:  make minikube-detect-cluster-cidrs
#      (or: deploy/scripts/minikube-detect-cluster-cidrs.sh)
#   2. Add the rendered file to `patchesStrategicMerge` in this overlay's
#      kustomization.yaml:  - patches/llm-egress-cluster-cidrs.yaml
# The rendered file is gitignored; only this template is tracked.
#
# CIDR FORMAT — comma-separated. CONTEXT_MAPPER_K8S_API_CIDRS is the kube-apiserver
# reachable ranges (on minikube the node /32 that fronts the apiserver, like the
# k8s-api-ip patch); it is validated by host-context-controller/src/k8sApiCidrs.ts,
# which rejects over-broad ranges at boot (an invalid placeholder here fails the
# pod — that is what keeps this patch opt-in). CONTEXT_MAPPER_CLUSTER_INTERNAL_CIDRS
# is the pod + Service CIDRs; it is passed as-is to the runtime LAN classifier
# (no over-broad rejection), so set it tightly — an over-broad range like
# 10.0.0.0/8 would swallow legitimate RFC1918 LAN targets as cluster-internal.
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: host-context-controller
  namespace: control-plane
spec:
  template:
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: host-context-controller
          env:
            - name: CONTEXT_MAPPER_K8S_API_CIDRS
              value: "__K8S_API_CIDRS__"
            - name: CONTEXT_MAPPER_CLUSTER_INTERNAL_CIDRS
              value: "__CLUSTER_INTERNAL_CIDRS__"
